# MS-COCO with uncropped test images: the explainer sees the original images of the 500 test
# entries (data/coco_common10/val/<class>/) instead of crops around the class's segmentation mask
# (val_masked/), so the test images keep the distribution of COCO. Test images and 2x2 grids are
# JSON lists (preprocessing/build_subset.py --source data/coco_common10 --out
# data/coco_common10/full_test --grids-only --seed 42); grids are composed in memory. Source after coco.env.
# Concepts (steps 1-5) do not use test images: scripts/run_experiments.py coco_full reuses the coco runs'.
IMAGE_ROOT_SINGLE=data/coco_common10/full_test/test.json
IMAGE_ROOT_GRID=data/coco_common10/full_test/grids.json
IMAGE_ROOT=${IMAGE_ROOT_SINGLE}
